Description:
Offline filter-list snapshots from The EasyList authors (https://easylist.to/).
The source snapshots, exact URLs, hashes and retrieval times are in upstream/
and sources.json. They are not executable code. The selected CC-BY-SA license
applies to this filter data and its derived lists.

Local Modifications:
build_rules.py deterministically removes comments and options with unsupported
side effects. It preserves network rules and bounded cosmetic candidates. Rust
independently admits only plain declarative hiding selectors, never scriptlets,
procedural actions or arbitrary styles. Exclusions are in rules_manifest.json.
Balanced uses EasyList plus TAHAI's baseline; Strict adds EasyPrivacy and the
TAHAI Strict additions. Lists update with the browser, without automatic fetches.
